<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eutin</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eutin is a town among the lakes of Holstein in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig-holstein">Schleswig-Holstein</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. From the 14th century it was the residence of the prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lubeck">Lübeck</a>, and later of the Oldenburg Principality of Lübeck. In the late 18th century its court attracted writers such as Johann Heinrich Voss, and the composer Carl Maria von Weber was born there in 1786.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eutin.jpg" alt="Eutin" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nordenfan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eutin_Schloss_Eingang.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
